# What must not reach the module repository.
#
# The repository is the distribution channel: whatever is published there is
# downloaded by the installations. Anything listed here is local to this
# installation, or of no use to whoever installs the module.

# Editor and operating-system leftovers.
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   module.json  — this is what identifies a folder of Custom/ as a managed
#                  module, and every module of the repository must carry one:
#                  upd_load_config() reads it, upd_list_modules() and
#                  upd_valid_module() use its presence as the test, and
#                  upd_install_module() downloads it from the repository when
#                  installing a sibling module. It holds no secret here: its
#                  github_token MUST stay empty in the committed copy. An
#                  administrator can set one locally without it ever coming
#                  back, because an existing module.json is never overwritten.
#   content/     — the courses are distributed, and have their own update
#                  channel on the administration screen.
